            "beta 15, beta 16 - First macOS version (Swift / SwiftUI): Tracking, Moon position, EME budget, Solar noise, general settings.",
            "beta 17 - \"IN-DEPTH CALCULATIONS\" box in Tracking (columns from Dpol onwards, intermediate rows of the EME budget, Solar noise tab); estimated S/N on the main screen; \"BAND SELECTION\" button with the bands from 50 MHz to 122 GHz.",
            "Top right: the \"IN-DEPTH CALCULATIONS\" box shows the columns from Dpol onwards in Moon position and all the rows of the EME budget (without the tick only the final row of each section is shown) and enables the Solar noise tab; the \"SHOW COMPLEX DATA ON THE MAIN SCREEN\" box shows the S/N estimated now at the bottom right; the \"BAND SELECTION\" button opens the list of bands to use in the calculations, from 50 MHz to 122 GHz.",
            "The Solar noise tab is enabled with the \"IN-DEPTH CALCULATIONS\" box in the Live position and +- 24h tab.",
            "Noise figure of the transverter in reception (dB). With transverter gain 0 the stage does not exist and this figure is not taken into account.",
            "Antenna temperature Ta in kelvin, as in VE7BQH's (Lionel Edwards) antenna performance tables: it includes side lobes, rear lobes, ground and internal losses, and is computed with the antenna tilted at 30° elevation.\nLook up your antenna (or a similar one) in the VE7BQH tables and enter here the Ta value for the band.\nIn the calculation: Tsys = Tant + (Tsky behind the Moon - reference Tsky, if positive) + Sun + receiver Te.",
