            "Yellow handles",
            "Aerial photo or topographic map centred on your station, with the sky dome drawn in plan on top (horizon = outer circle, zenith = centre): current Moon position, path over the next 24 hours with rise and set, antenna limits in yellow and the areas outside the limits blurred in light grey. Drag the yellow handles with the mouse to adjust the limits directly on the map; the wheel changes the zoom.",
