            "Effective area",
            "{0} ({1}) is in the polar cap: after strong solar proton events there may be PCA (Polar Cap Absorption), an absorption of the lower ionosphere that can last a few days.",
            "{0} ({1}) is in the auroral zone (geomagnetic latitude {2:F0}°): during geomagnetic storms there may be auroral absorption.",
            "Absorption decreases with frequency (roughly 1/f²): it matters mostly at 50 MHz, less at 144 MHz, and is usually negligible from 432 MHz upwards. Current frequency: {0} MHz.",
            "The current situation can be checked with the NOAA D-RAP service: https://www.swpc.noaa.gov/products/d-region-absorption-predictions-d-rap",
